sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P as Programmer
    participant UI as Track Controller UI (QML)
    participant S as TrackControllerState
    participant C as plc
    participant W as TrackController (wayside)
    participant U as Program (user)
    participant V as Program (vital code)
    P->>UI: click Run
    UI->>S: run()
    alt no track loaded
        S->>S: run internal: _log(load a track first)
        S-->>UI: emit terminalChanged
    else a wayside is selected
        S->>C: compile_program(buffer)
        C-->>S: return Program, with its diagnostics
        S->>W: diagnose(program)
        W->>W: diagnose internal: program.diagnostics + check_program(program)
        Note right of W: check_program: every name is this wayside's I/O and every output is driven.
        W-->>S: return the diagnostics
        alt has_errors(diagnostics)
            S-->>UI: emit bufferChanged: parser pane, compile failed
        else compiles
            S->>W: trial(program)
            W->>W: trial internal: copy.copy(self) with its own input card
            W->>W: _run internal: build_scan_inputs() on the copy (OS decode)
            W->>U: scan(image)
            U-->>W: return (values, warnings)
            W->>V: scan(image + the program's outputs)
            V-->>W: return the final OUT_ bits
            W->>W: _run internal: encode_outputs(final), report_overrides(...), _format_log()
            W-->>S: return the trial copy: track_circuits, overrides, warnings, log
            S->>S: run internal: verified := buffer only if there is no diagnostic
            S-->>UI: emit bufferChanged, terminalChanged
            UI-->>P: sandbox outputs, log, overrides. Commit enabled only after a clean run.
        end
    end
    Note over S,V: trial scans a copy of the wayside. The live outputs, the committed program and the track are untouched.
